    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n23/10/2026 - 12:00\n\nFOR SALE BY LIVE STREAM PROPERTY AUCTION, FRIDAY 23rd OCTOBER AT 12.00 NOON.\n\nO'Donnellan & Joyce are delighted to present this exceptional countryside estate to the market, nestled within a truly idyllic and scenic setting in the heart of Connemara.\n\n\"Beal an Atha\" is a distinctive farmhouse-style residence occupying a magnificent site extending to approximately 2.47 acres. While the main dwelling would benefit from refurbishment and modernisation, it presents an outstanding opportunity to create a superb family home or to explore a range of potential commercial uses, subject to the necessary consents.\n\nExtending to approximately 176 sq.m. (1,894 sq.ft.) over ground and first floor levels, the residence offers generous accommodation throughout. Adjoining the main house is a substantial workshop extending to approximately 60 sq.m. (646 sq.ft.), complete with independent access, providing excellent flexibility for a variety of uses. To the rear of the property, there is a range of traditional outbuildings suitable for storage, workshop space, or further conversion potential, subject to planning permission.\n\nA charming tree-lined avenue leads to a detached two-storey stone outbuilding, formerly utilised as agricultural stables. Rich in character and heritage, this attractive structure retains many original features, including natural stone walls and chimney breasts, offering tremendous scope for restoration and alternative uses.\n\nIdeally positioned along the R336 Coastal Route, the property enjoys a highly accessible location just 1 km from Connemara Airport and within 3 km of TG4, Tully Business Park, and a host of local amenities and services.\n\nOne of the property's most compelling attributes is its spectacular setting and unrivalled panoramic views. From the residence, one can enjoy breathtaking vistas across Galway Bay, The Burren, and all three Aran Islands, creating a truly unique living environment rarely found on the market.\n\n\"Beal an Atha\" represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial holding with exceptional character, remarkable redevelopment potential, and some of the most stunning coastal views that Connemara has to offer.\n\nSOLICITOR WITH CARRIAGE OF SALE: Ms. Susan Egan, Blake & Kenny Solicitors, 2 Saint Francis Street, Galway, H91 CA37\n\nAUCTION PROCESS \n\nPre-Registration Required in Order to Bid By Phone or Online. Please familiarize yourself with the Auction Process prior to bidding.\n\nPlease note the following: 5,000 bidder security fee must be paid in advance to bid on the day (if unsuccessful this is fully refunded to you) If you are successful, you are immediately contracted on the drop of the hammer and the non-refundable balance of 10% must be paid immediately. \nPhone and Online bidding service available you must pre-register to bid prior to Auction Day - you can register on our website under the auction tab at top of the homepage. \n\nRegister for legals on our website under the auction tab at top of the homepage (please note all legals may not be available for download until closer to the auction date - once you have registered you will receive an alert when they do become available). We always advise potential purchasers to have their solicitor review legals prior to bidding.\n\nFor Further details please contact O'Donnellan & Joyce on 091-564212 \n\nOFFICE OPENING HOURS - MON TO FRI 9AM TO 5:30PM\n\n\nNOTE: These particulars are not to be considered a formal offer. They are for information only and give a general idea of the property. They are not to be taken as forming any part of a resulting contract, nor to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. \n\nNo person in the employment of O'Donnellan & Joyce Auctioneers has any authority to make or give any representation or warranty whatever in relation to this property.\n\nNote: Prospective purchasers must satisfy themselves as to the condition and suitability of the property, its existing or potential use, any development or redevelopment potential, any necessary planning permissions or other consents, and as to the availability of and eligibility of the property and/or any prospective purchaser for any grants, schemes or funding. No representation or warranty is made or given by or on behalf of the Vendor in relation to any such matters."
      },
      {
